{"quote_id":"TS-CUR-001","corpus_id":"B006","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Search","source_year":1946,"source_slug":"the_search","source_section":"Complete monograph","quote_original":"Whatever we conceive It as being, that It is to us.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["SPIRITUAL"],"tags":["conception","inner-self","perception"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_search.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"TS-CUR-002","corpus_id":"B006","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Search","source_year":1946,"source_slug":"the_search","source_section":"Complete monograph","quote_original":"My mystical experiences have convinced me that there is no way to bring about the outer perfection we seek other than by the transformation of ourselves.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"],"tags":["transformation","self-concept","change"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_search.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"TS-CUR-003","corpus_id":"B006","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Search","source_year":1946,"source_slug":"the_search","source_section":"Complete monograph","quote_original":"What we imagine, that we are.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["imagination","identity","being"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_search.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"TS-CUR-004","corpus_id":"B006","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Search","source_year":1946,"source_slug":"the_search","source_section":"Complete monograph","quote_original":"Nothing is more important to us than our conception of ourselves, and especially is this true of our concept of the deep, hidden One within us.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["SPIRITUAL"],"tags":["self-concept","identity","inner-self"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_search.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"TS-CUR-005","corpus_id":"B006","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Search","source_year":1946,"source_slug":"the_search","source_section":"Complete monograph","quote_original":"It is our conception of ourselves which frees or constrains us, though it may use material agencies to achieve its purpose.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["STATES"],"tags":["self-concept","freedom","limitation"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_search.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"TS-CUR-006","corpus_id":"B006","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Search","source_year":1946,"source_slug":"the_search","source_section":"Complete monograph","quote_original":"No help cometh from without; the hills to which we lift our eyes are those of an inner range.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["within","consciousness","inner-source"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_search.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"TS-CUR-007","corpus_id":"B006","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Search","source_year":1946,"source_slug":"the_search","source_section":"Complete monograph","quote_original":"To attempt to change the world before we change our concept of ourselves is to struggle against the nature of things.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"],"tags":["self-concept","world","change"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_search.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"TS-CUR-008","corpus_id":"B006","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"The Search","source_year":1946,"source_slug":"the_search","source_section":"Complete monograph","quote_original":"Everything we do, unaccompanied by a change of consciousness, is but futile readjustment of surfaces.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["consciousness","change","inner-state"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_the_search.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
